## VS CODE REMOTE DEVELOPMENT
1. Open VS Code
2. Install the Remote-SSH extension
3. Press ctrl+shift+P; then Remote-SSH:Connect to Host"
4. Enter pi@trio or use IP address
5. Open folder /home/pi/thesis

## SENSOR CODE
1. Project Structure
~/rice-paddy-monitor/
├── venv/
├── models/
│   └── your-edge-impulse-model.eim
├── src/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── sensors.py
│   ├── camera.py
│   ├── inference.py
│   └── main.py
├── config/
│   └── settings.py
├── logs/
├── data/
└── requirements.txt

2. Create the structure
  cd~/thesis
  mkdir -p src config logs data models
  touch src/_init_.py

3. Configurate File

"""
Configuration settings for Rice Paddy Monitoring System
Modify these values for your specific setup
"""

# Sensor Configuration
DHT_PIN = 4  # GPIO pin for DHT22 data
SOIL_MOISTURE_CHANNEL = 0  # ADS1115 channel (A0)

# Soil moisture calibration values
# Measure these with your actual sensor:
# - SOIL_DRY: ADC value when sensor is in dry air
# - SOIL_WET: ADC value when sensor is submerged in water
SOIL_DRY = 20000   # Typical dry value (adjust after calibration)
SOIL_WET = 8000    # Typical wet value (adjust after calibration)

# Camera Configuration
CAMERA_INDEX = 0  # Usually 0 for USB webcam
CAMERA_WIDTH = 640
CAMERA_HEIGHT = 480

# Edge Impulse Model
MODEL_PATH = "/home/pi/thesis/models/your-model.eim"

# Data Logging
LOG_INTERVAL_SECONDS = 300  # Log sensor data every 5 minutes
DATA_DIR = "/home/pi/thesis/data"
LOG_DIR = "/home/pi/thesis/logs"

# Thresholds for alerts (adjust based on rice paddy requirements)
TEMP_MIN = 20.0  # Celsius
TEMP_MAX = 35.0
HUMIDITY_MIN = 60.0  # Percent
HUMIDITY_MAX = 90.0
SOIL_MOISTURE_MIN = 40.0  # Percent (paddy rice needs wet soil)

